  "output": {
    "answer": "In my process, whoever owns the product is the one who decides whether a NOT is a simple fix to make inline or something pervasive enough to re-run the panel. Disagreements get settled by naming the design principle behind each side, never by majority vote or by deferring to my own ask — and refusals are logged explicitly, with the reasoning attached, rather than complied with silently. So yes, the panel's verdict can be declined; the record just requires writing down why when that happens.",
